{
  "$comment": "What would prove each element RAN, not merely deployed (#325). The class this answers has three known members -- Loop Marker ran ONCE where it should have run three times; Manual Task and Task (Generic) pass straight through creating nothing -- and all three were found by a person, not a test.",
  "$status": "MEASURED, partially. `provenByStartingAnInstance` is the result of DEPLOYING a minimal process per element, STARTING an instance, and observing the declared effect -- 19 of the 20 elements with a declared effect are proven this way by tools/bpmn-execution-probe/probe.py. The 20th, Service Task (Behavior), runs its behaviour as an HTTP callback into the Auton8 app and so cannot be proven by the engine alone. The 37 elements with declaredEffect null are NOT proven and AC3 makes that a finding rather than a pass; the seven with an empty liveEngineTestsMentioningIt are #404.",
  "$why-not-in-bpmn-support": "An observable effect is an axis bpmn-support.json does not have, and #324 already rejected bolting a column onto 69 rows to serve a subset.",
  "$fields": {
    "declaredEffect": "task-appears | variable-written | instance-waits | instance-ends, or null where no unambiguous effect has been declared yet -- which AC3 makes a FINDING, not a pass",
    "liveEngineTestsMentioningIt": "E2E classes whose source contains this element's construct. A mention is weaker than an assertion; an EMPTY list is the strong signal.",
    "provenByStartingAnInstance": "true when an instance was started and the declared effect was observed. Absent means no effect is declared, so nothing was attempted.",
    "measured": "what the engine actually showed, verbatim from the probe"
  },
